  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-10-18T17:12:30.407Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's historically been a bit iffy to include output logs on public canny posts due to them containing detailed records about your movements (including instance IDs that could be used to join those instances). However, it's now much worse - on both live and 1001, output logs contain _all of your friend movements_ - complete with the instance IDs they are moving to. This needs to be redacted; people should not be encouraged to put output logs on gist when they're going to out everything their friends are doing.",
